From 6bc34a231ff64a89cda30e23a978ac323e6d0893 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:27:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] lifecycle guard: read uv value options,
 leading/glued `<`, cat's stdin and piped groups

Review 5892368091 on #2233 found commands the lifecycle guard still allowed although they
run a file that restarts the gateway. Base allowed them too, so none is a regression:

1. `_UV_VALUE_OPTIONS` lacked `-w` (short `--with`), `--upgrade-group`, the `--*-package`
   value options and the hidden `--python-preference`. `uv run -w requests f.py` read
   `requests` as the command and never opened f.py. The tables now follow `uv help run`
   (uv 0.13.7): value options and flags, with short clusters read like getopt (`-qw x`).
   An option neither table knows is read both ways, flag first (the old reading), then
   taking a value, and every reading's command is scanned. So `uv run --new-opt v f.py`
   and `uv --new-global v run f.py` fail closed. `uv run -` (program on stdin, verified
   with uv 0.13.7) now scans its stdin and pipe feeds. The uv argv reader moved to
   cron/lifecycle_guard_uv.py so lifecycle_guard.py stays under its line cap.
2. Stdin feeds the segment walk missed:
   - leading redirection `< f.py python3`, `sudo < f.sh bash`;
   - glued redirection `python3<f.py`, `bash<f.sh` (`<` is not a control char);
   - `cat < f.py | python3` (cat's own stdin was dropped);
   - `cat f.py | (python3)`, `| (true; bash)`, `| { true; bash; }` (the `(` reset the
     pipe feed; a group's commands all inherit its stdin).
   `_command_segment_views` adds a view with command-position redirections moved to the
   end (a shell applies them wherever they appear). Like the keyword-peeled view, it only
   adds a reading. Only the command word is split at a glued `<`/`>`; arguments are never
   split, so `bash -c 'python3<f.py'` keeps its payload whole for the recursive scan.
   `_iter_segment_contexts` keeps a stack of the feed each `(`/`{` group inherited.

Proof:
- tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_stdin_feeds.py at base 0d81fe01f8 (#2233 head): 50
  failed, 23 passed. Every must-refuse case is red there except three already-correct
  controls (`uv run -wrequests`, `uv run --with=requests`, `cat f.py | { python3; }`), and
  every mention/data case is green. At this head all 73 pass, and
  test_lifecycle_guard_interpreter_runners.py (mention/data guards included) stays green.
- Mutants (sdlc-review mutants.py, 27 edits over every added condition): 26 killed; the one
  first survivor (alternate index past the end) is now killed by a unit test. Removed one
  redundant branch and one dead guard that left equivalent mutants.
- scripts/run_tests.sh tests/cron/ plus the heredoc background guard, the approval parity,
  hermes-sync hint, execute_code deadline and gateway restart/lifecycle guard suites:
  2868 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped.
